INT. ARLO'S APARTMENT - ENTRY HALL - NIGHT

Dark. A key rattles in the lock. The door swings inward, bumping a stack of unopened mail.

ARLO PENDERGAST (40s, rain-soaked suit, a cake box under one arm, a party hat still on his head from a party that ended badly) steps inside. He closes the door with his heel. Flips the switch.

Nothing.

                    ARLO
          Of course.

He fumbles in the dark. Finds the wall. Finds a plant. Apologizes to the plant.

                    ARLO (CONT'D)
          Sorry.

The red light of an answering machine blinks on a side table. He stares at it. He presses PLAY.

                    ARLO (V.O.)
                (answering machine, cheerful)
          Hi! You've reached Arlo. I'm either out having an amazing time or I'm in the bath. Leave a message!

A long beep. Silence. Arlo (the real one) exhales through his nose.

He sets the cake box on the table. Opens it. Inside, a small cake, the frosting smeared, a single candle bent sideways. The words "HAPPY 40TH" have slid into "HAPPY 4 TH."

                    ARLO
          Happy 4th.

He picks up the candle. Lights it with a match from his pocket. The flame illuminates his face from below, hollow-eyed, absurd under the paper hat.

He sits on the floor. Tilts the cake toward himself. Takes a breath to blow it out.

The answering machine clicks. Another message.

                    ARLO (V.O.)
                (answering machine, slightly drunk)
          Hey, it's me. Future me. Just wanted to say, whatever you wished for, you're welcome.

Arlo sits perfectly still. The candle burns down.

He laughs. First small, then helpless, then in great wheezing gasps, tears running into the party hat's elastic. He blows out the candle, sits in the smoke, and eats the cake with his fingers.
